    "summary": "An annual herb native to the Mediterranean area and Western Europe, including northern Africa, Turkey, Iran and eastern North Atlantic islands. Its thin, branching stems carry rings of narrow leaves and tiny greenish-white or purple-tinged flowers; hooked bristles densely cover the fruit. It readily occupies rocky habitats and old stone walls.",
